so I really went back and forth about  whether to even do this story today  about how there still is no connection  between undocumented immigrants and  criminality because on the one hand  we've already covered this story it's  sort of obvious that this is the case  but there are still so many people who  believe deeply believe that undocumented  immigrants are more likely to commit  crimes in the United States so  ultimately I made the case that it is  worth debunking once again and before I  even tell you about the new report let's  just remind ourselves of some of the  obvious realities coming to the United  States illegally is illegal it can be a  misdemeanor or a civil infraction  depending on whether you've overstayed a  visa or are crossing the border without  permission that's not what's at issue  here okay what is that issue here is  whether undocumented immigrants do or do  not commit more crime than native-born  Americans or more crime than legal  immigrants to the United States and we  hear a lot of specific anecdotes from  Donald Trump and right-wingers who have  propagandized around this about crimes  committed by undocumented immigrants and  of course in a country this big there  are examples of everything but this is  important because our policy towards  immigration would be different depending  on whether or not undocumented  immigrants actually are more likely to  commit violent crime and property crime  in the United States but this is pretty  obvious undocumented immigrants know  that they are undocumented they know  that if they get into trouble with the  authorities if they come to the  attention of law enforcement not only  could they suffer the penalties for the  crime that they commit but they could be  deported they could get in trouble for  being undocumented so why would a group  that knows they have an extra incentive  to stay off the radar of law enforcement  why would they commit crimes at a higher  rate than native-born Americans and  legal immigrants and attract the  attention of law enforcement yes we know  that poverty and crime are connected  many undocumented immigrants are poor  but the research has shown for a long  time that undocumented immigrants aren't  more likely to be violent criminals and  yet again we have a new study with  Pew data Pew Research Center data  analyzed by the Marshall project what  tells us that undocumented immigrants  don't increase crime rates whether or  not undocumented immigration to a metro  area increased the crime rates have  continued to slowly decline more or less  equally and in fact there are many areas  with more undocumented immigration that  have had even larger decreases in crime  even though it's by a small amount and  maybe not statistically significant now  this is not to argue that we shouldn't  deal with undocumented immigration which  is still a crime right although it's  only a civil infraction or a misdemeanor  again depending on whether you're  talking about an overstayed  crossing the border without permission  but we cannot allow this discussion to  be framed as we have a crisis of violent  undocumented immigrants in the United  States because we don't and this is  actually the epitome of how the  Republican Party often very successfully  influences public opinion the principle  is they take an anecdote and they  exploit it to make people scared or  angry and to eventually support bad  policy policy that doesn't actually make  sense so let me do an analogy first to  abortion they come out they say extreme  late term abortions have to be stopped  Democrats are killing babies this is  horrible when you look at it you realize  wait a second extreme late term abortion  is really rare and when it's something  that takes place the baby often is going  to die anyway within days or weeks of of  coming out of the uterus and it more  becomes a question of the life of the  mother it becomes a question of how soon  is this fetus going to be determined  non-viable but Republicans use the  strawman of the post birth abortion and  all of these crazy things to justify  trying to ban abortion altogether this  is the same thing going on with with  undocumented immigration and illegal as  they like to say killed this person well  that's a crime it's a tragedy  it's horrifying okay I I would not even  think of minimizing the [ __ ]  nature of that but the real discussion  around undocumented immigration is is  not actually about crime it's about  economics it's about culture it's about  geopolitics  it's about diplomacy and Foreign  Relations and foreign policy that's the  real conversation around undocumented  immigration and the problem is that if  you actually have the conversation on  those terms instead of about these  crimes that Donald Trump and others like  to point to the outcome the right path  forward becomes one that the American  right simply doesn't want it becomes one  of working to minimize the circumstances  in the source countries of undocumented  immigration that make people want to  come here to begin with  it becomes an issue of dealing with the  economic conditions and the large  corporations that are actually a big  driver for that undocumented immigration  because they are employing undocumented  immigrants if you actually deal with  undocumented immigration as an economic  cultural and geopolitical issue you  can't justify the policies that  Republicans want which is why they have  to couch it in these terms of dangerous  brown people coming over the border yet  another study tells us it's absolutely  ridiculous
 

